  "content_description": "Career Action Item",
  "content_text_body": "Schedule a meeting with your team where your goal is to understand how each team member can approach learning and how they can help each other grow at work. As the manager, you'll both facilitate and participate in the discussion.\n\n### Prior to the discussion\n\nUnderstand clearly what Growth Mindset means and why it's important.\n\nPeople with a Growth Mindset (versus a Fixed Mindset) believe that their intelligence, skills and talents can improve through hard work, new experiences and even failures.\n\nCheck out the Resources page to learn more about Growth Mindsets.\n\n### Team discussion on Growth Mindset\n\nBegin by going over the [Meeting Ground Rules](Glint_General_Team_Meeting_Ground_Rules).\n\nFollow this [Meeting Plan](Glint_Career_Growth_Mindset_Meeting_Plan) to guide your discussion.",
